      "content": "Stress can indeed cause what feels like gaps or moments of intense confusion. While vitamins and melatonin might help if your issue is related to sleep or nutrient deficiencies, they may not fully address your brain fog if it's primarily due to stress. I recommend starting with stress-management techniques such as meditation or exercise. However, incorporating a balanced diet and possibly consulting with a healthcare provider is always a good idea to rule out any potential deficiencies or underlying conditions.",
