      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to be hesitant about healthcare costs, especially if your symptoms are mild and don't seem to be lasting long. Monitoring how you feel and implementing lifestyle changes could be a good initial step. That said, keeping an eye on these symptoms and seeking professional advice could still be beneficial in the long run. It's better to identify any possible underlying issues early rather than having them potentially worsen. If you're concerned about cost, you might look into your local healthcare services to see if there are affordable clinics or services available to you.",
      "source": "target",
